==English==
{{was wotd|2011|June|23}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|phōca||seal}} (from {{der|en|grc|φώκη}}) {{suffix|en||ine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfəʊsʌɪn/|/ˈfəʊsiːn/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phocine.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Pertaining to a [[seal]] (or similar [[pinniped]]s); [[seallike]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=28 December 1871|journal=New York Daily Standard|text=He telegraphed to the whaling ports of New England, and sent messages to San Francisco and Alaska, to know if a group of sea lions and other specimens of the '''phocine''' tribe could be secured.}}
#* {{RQ:Nabokov Lolita|page=44|text={{...}} she had already yanked out of me the coveted section [of the newspaper] and retreated to her mat near her '''phocine''' mamma.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987|author={{w|William Boyd (writer)|William Boyd}}|title=The New Confessions|text=She walked over towards me with an odd elegance, big strides, like a champion girl swimmer, say; muscled but lean, with a '''phocine''' grace.}}

